# Recorded terminal demos (docs/demo/) are binary artifacts that get re-cut
# whenever the CLI output they show changes. Storing them in LFS keeps each
# revision out of the regular object stack, so a clone does not carry every
# past recording.
#
# Contributors need `git lfs install` once; without it these paths check out as
# ~130-byte pointer files and the docs render with broken images.
docs/demo/*.gif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
